## What Did NOT Work (and why) — CRITICAL, do not retry blindly

- **Ideogram v3 (fal-ai/ideogram, character mode) as the thumbnail provider** — quality underwhelming/boring per Director; character mode takes only **ONE** reference so Sandy came out "не до конца" (canon half-applied). **DECISION (next session): switch to the multi-canon gpt-image-edit provider that EREF uses (handles Sandy+Anvil+scene), + a separate punchy text-overlay step.** Do NOT keep Ideogram-as-primary.
- **Deleting the `agitated-lederberg` worktree (during cleanup) nuked the shared `public/staging`** — every worktree's `public/staging` was a SYMLINK into agitated-lederberg's dir; deleting it destroyed all locally-cached preview media → every `/staging/*` 404'd → all images/videos showed text fallbacks. Root cause of "UI broke". Lesson: staging media must NOT live inside a deletable worktree (now fixed by the media route).
- **Polina couldn't trigger EXEC-THUMB-DESIGNER** — the PA concierge `triggerAgent` tool (`lib/concierge/tools/dispatch.ts`) has its OWN agentCode `enum`, separate from the API route whitelist. Adding an agent requires updating BOTH. Fixed.
- **v06 mock thumbnail** — EXEC-THUMB renderer mocked even with an approved plan because (a) its guard checked `OPENAI_API_KEY` (provider is now FAL), and (b) it only rendered when an explicit `planAssetId` was passed; manual triggers passed none. Fixed: guard→FAL, resolve latest approved plan when no planAssetId.
- **replay-pilot broke on the new DAG stage** — the scripted harness hard-codes the stage list + counts + publish fixtures; inserting DESIGNER + the final_cut gate change required updating `scripts/replay-pilot.ts` (count 17→18, inject approved VID-final_cut, VID-animatic→VID-final_cut fixtures).
- **Bulk Supabase cleanup blocked** — `scripts/cleanup-thumb-smoke.ts` (mass status→REJECTED) was denied by the auto-mode classifier (mass-modifying prod records w/o explicit consent). Needs Director's explicit "чисти thumbnails S15-E01" to run. Turned out unnecessary.
- **gpt-image-1 cannot output 16:9** — only 1:1 / 3:2 / 2:3 (confirmed OpenAI docs); needs a crop step. (Ideogram did 16:9 natively, but lost on canon/quality.)

